# Manifest defaults must be realistic (R5)

`app-config.toml` manifests carry two defaults per key: `default_dev`
(used by `cargo run` and the dev resolver) and `default_prod` (used by
MSI / RPM / notarized-pkg installs). The audit found `default_dev`
entries that were stale placeholders (`server.example.com`,
`12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012`, `my-test-tenant`), so a fresh
developer's first "Test connectivity" click failed even though both
halves of the dev stack were healthy.

## The rule

> **Every `default_dev` must be a value that lets the reference dev
> smoke loop — `cargo build` → MSI install → configurator
> Test-connectivity — pass without operator edits. The reference dev
> stack is: `pim-offline-server` on `https://localhost:8443/`, the dev
> TLS cert from `core-assets/certs/localhost-dev/`, default Postgres on
> `localhost:5432` with the bootstrap credentials from
> `pim-installers/dev/postgres.env`. If a `default_dev` cannot satisfy
> that loop (a required secret, a per-tenant GUID, a deployment-specific
> field), leave the value empty AND document the requirement in two
> places: (a) the `# operator must set before first run` comment in the
> manifest, and (b) the configurator's first-run banner listing "fields
> you must set before Save".**

`default_prod` may legitimately stay empty for values requiring operator
input; the smoke-loop half of the rule applies only to `default_dev`.

## Reference dev stack (keep in sync when the stack moves)

| Component | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Offline server (TLS) | `https://localhost:8443/` |
| Offline server (plain / health) | `http://localhost:8080/` |
| Server TLS bundle | `core-assets/certs/localhost-dev/server.{crt,key}` (synced by `pim-installers/scripts/Sync-DevCerts.ps1`) |
| Dev CA | `core-assets/certs/localhost-dev/dev-ca.crt` |
| Postgres host / port / db | `localhost` / `5432` / `pim_offline_dev` |
| Postgres user / password | from `pim-installers/dev/postgres.env` (development only, never committed) |
| Default tenant name | `Default Tenant` |
| Default tenant GUID | empty — operator chooses (R6) |

## Required patterns

Useful default when possible:

```toml
[[key]]
name = "SERVER_PUBLIC_URL"
value_type = "string"
default_dev = "https://localhost:8443"
default_prod = ""            # operator MUST set before first run
description = "Base URL the offline server advertises in installation JSON."
operator_must_set = true
```

Empty default plus first-run banner when the value cannot be guessed:

```toml
[[key]]
name = "AGENT_UUID"
value_type = "string"
default_dev = ""             # operator must set before first run
default_prod = ""
description = "Stable identity supplied by the operator at install."
operator_must_set = true     # surfaces in the first-run banner
```

Configurator GUIs read `operator_must_set = true` and render a "Fields
you must set before Save" banner on first run, enumerating those keys in
manifest order with click-to-focus per row. Save with any such field
still empty fails with an inline error naming the field — no toast, and
the field stays highlighted.

## Forbidden constructs

- `default_dev` naming any `.example` / `.test` / `.invalid` hostname —
  the dev stack does not run there.
- `default_dev` set to a placeholder GUID (also banned by R6; empty is
  the only sentinel).
- `default_dev` containing `changeme` / `do-not-ship` / `test-secret` /
  `my-test-tenant` or any other string the runtime fingerprinter (R7)
  flags.
- `default_dev = "0.0.0.0"` for a **connect** target (bind targets are
  fine).
- `default_prod` naming `localhost` for a value an MSI install will have
  no localhost service for (LDAP, KDC, …).
- A `default_prod` that is a copy of a realistic `default_dev` — that
  leaks dev endpoints into prod installs.

## Reference dev smoke loop (manual verification)

```powershell
cd c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-client;  cargo build
cd c:\analog-pim\pim-installers;      pwsh .\scripts\Build-PimOfflineAgentMsi.ps1
msiexec /i .\dist\AIC-OfflinePimAgent.msi /qb
cd c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-server;  cargo run       # separate window
& "$env:ProgramFiles\AIC\OfflinePimAgent\pim-offline-client-configurator-win32.exe"
# Settings -> Server Connection -> Test connectivity
```

Every substep (parse / DNS / TCP / TLS / app handshake) must succeed
with no field edited first. Profile follows
[`development-mode-debug-builds.mdc`](development-mode-debug-builds.mdc).

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** `default_dev = "https://server.example.com:8443"` for
`SERVER_PUBLIC_URL` (and the same value copied into `default_prod`).
Test connectivity fails on a fresh install because the hostname does not
resolve.

**Fix:** `default_dev = "https://localhost:8443"`, `default_prod = ""`
with `operator_must_set = true`. The dev loop passes on first click; the
prod installer flags the field in the first-run banner.

